WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.910
- If you're parented well, you
can see if from a mile away,

00:00:03.910 --> 00:00:05.800
and when you're not you
can see it from a mile away

00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:10.103
and I think too many parents
view their kids as a product.

00:00:14.990 --> 00:00:17.910
We need to do a much
better job, zero to 18

00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:20.020
to understand somebody's makeup,

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:22.630
their emotional makeup, their skill set.

00:00:22.630 --> 00:00:23.910
The way we do school today

00:00:23.910 --> 00:00:26.040
and the way we structure
our kids for success

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:29.190
in the first 18 years
is so broken, worldwide.

00:00:29.190 --> 00:00:32.570
For a lot of parent, their kid
is a representation of them,

00:00:32.570 --> 00:00:33.720
and that's where it breaks.

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:37.010
It breaks if a parent thinks
that a kids accomplishment

00:00:37.010 --> 00:00:40.470
is a reflection them, because
now you have a disconnect.

00:00:40.470 --> 00:00:42.800
Now you're not a parent and a child,

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:44.830
you're a person with a product

00:00:44.830 --> 00:00:48.340
and I think, that, that is scary to me,

00:00:48.340 --> 00:00:51.491
because going to Harvard,
or Stanford, or Yale,

00:00:51.491 --> 00:00:54.440
is a badge that people back in Beijing

00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:57.240
walk around proudly to
their contemporaries

00:00:57.240 --> 00:00:59.210
and they're fuckin' their kids up.

00:00:59.210 --> 00:01:00.960
If you look at America as a proxy,

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:02.860
when the middle class started to emerge

00:01:02.860 --> 00:01:04.740
it was also when University and college

00:01:04.740 --> 00:01:06.490
was starting to build as a brand

00:01:06.490 --> 00:01:09.320
and it worked for a period
of time, that was fine,

00:01:09.320 --> 00:01:12.000
but the problem is technology
is to much of a variable.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:13.750
If you want your kids to be successful,

00:01:13.750 --> 00:01:15.540
recognize that the world you live in today

00:01:15.540 --> 00:01:17.900
has nothing to do with the
world their gonna live in.

00:01:17.900 --> 00:01:18.733
- That's so true.

00:01:18.733 --> 00:01:20.950
- I had parents who had
those same pressures,

00:01:20.950 --> 00:01:22.630
who came from those same places,

00:01:22.630 --> 00:01:24.960
who refuse to treat me that way,

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:26.920
and that's why I'm gonna be special.

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:30.680
I want that for the gadrillions
of kids around the world,

00:01:30.680 --> 00:01:31.800
because they deserve it.

00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:36.019
The fact that 99 out of 100
parents back in Chinese New Year

00:01:36.019 --> 00:01:38.780
put unneeded pressure on their kids,

00:01:38.780 --> 00:01:41.540
which ultimately is going
to hurt their children

00:01:41.540 --> 00:01:43.900
and hurt their relationship
with their children

00:01:43.900 --> 00:01:46.330
is, needs to start being eradicated

00:01:46.330 --> 00:01:47.163
- One things happening.

00:01:47.163 --> 00:01:48.197
- Please.

00:01:48.197 --> 00:01:49.520
- In China that is an optimism,

00:01:49.520 --> 00:01:51.110
it's very optimistic point of view

00:01:51.110 --> 00:01:54.790
is the government is now
encouraging graduates

00:01:54.790 --> 00:01:57.260
to take entrepreneurship
as their first job.

00:01:57.260 --> 00:01:58.093
- I think it's great

00:01:58.093 --> 00:01:59.810
that it's pushing kids
to entrepreneurship.

00:01:59.810 --> 00:02:03.990
My problem is, nine out of
10 of these Chinese kids

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:04.990
that are 22 years olds,

00:02:04.990 --> 00:02:07.229
that are jumping into
entrepreneurship have no chance,

00:02:07.229 --> 00:02:08.810
'cause they're not entrepreneurs.

00:02:08.810 --> 00:02:10.889
- Yes, but it's good,
because it's education.

00:02:10.889 --> 00:02:13.160
- Yes, but you have to be careful

00:02:13.160 --> 00:02:17.490
because the one thing I fear,
is when theses kids fail

00:02:17.490 --> 00:02:18.929
and almost all of them will,

00:02:18.929 --> 00:02:22.620
it's a very big scarlet
letter in that culture,

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:23.930
and I think psychologically,

00:02:23.930 --> 00:02:27.270
you're putting a 23 year old
in a very vulnerable spot

00:02:27.270 --> 00:02:30.600
where now they have a loss,
publicly, there's no hiding.

00:02:30.600 --> 00:02:33.430
When you lose in school like
I did, you can blame people.

00:02:33.430 --> 00:02:36.050
When Iris loses at Vayner
Media she can blame me.

00:02:36.050 --> 00:02:37.300
When you work at a company,

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:39.487
or when the governments
involved, or when it's school,

00:02:39.487 --> 00:02:41.080
you can blame somebody else.

00:02:41.080 --> 00:02:43.310
When you have a business, it's your fault.

00:02:43.310 --> 00:02:47.090
So I would caution one thing
for anybody who's listening

00:02:47.090 --> 00:02:49.440
who thinks entrepreneurship
is such a freedom.

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:52.840
When you lose, you have to make sure

00:02:52.840 --> 00:02:54.110
that you're mentally stable enough

00:02:54.110 --> 00:02:56.430
to be able to take all that cynicism

00:02:56.430 --> 00:02:58.320
and the critiques from everybody,

00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:01.260
including your friends, your
friends parents, your parents,

00:03:01.260 --> 00:03:03.110
because if you don't you start going down

00:03:03.110 --> 00:03:07.120
a very dangerous path that
leads to a very scary place.

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:11.010
We do not reconcile why
we have suicide in America

00:03:11.010 --> 00:03:12.240
at the teenage level.

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:13.710
It's because modern parenting

00:03:13.710 --> 00:03:17.140
is over coddling kids to an extreme level

00:03:17.140 --> 00:03:19.680
where kids don't know how
to deal with adversity.

00:03:19.680 --> 00:03:21.750
I think self awareness matters much more

00:03:21.750 --> 00:03:22.998
than being an entrepreneur.

00:03:22.998 --> 00:03:26.480
For you and I the learning
makes sense, it's our DNA.

00:03:26.480 --> 00:03:28.360
I look at every loss as learning.

00:03:28.360 --> 00:03:30.490
That is not how people are wired.

00:03:30.490 --> 00:03:33.440
We need to do a much
better job zero to 18,

00:03:33.440 --> 00:03:35.160
to understand somebody's makeup.

00:03:35.160 --> 00:03:37.625
- To go deeper there
are a lot of new family,

00:03:37.625 --> 00:03:39.850
they just newly became the middle class.

00:03:39.850 --> 00:03:41.430
So the middle class is booming.

00:03:41.430 --> 00:03:43.580
So they're afraid that their gonna lose,

00:03:43.580 --> 00:03:45.410
because they just got there.

00:03:45.410 --> 00:03:48.377
The only way that they can
think of to maintain this status

00:03:48.377 --> 00:03:51.300
is to invest in their kids education,

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:53.310
or push a little bit harder to make sure

00:03:53.310 --> 00:03:55.257
their kids can carry on the status.

00:03:55.257 --> 00:03:56.090
- [Gary] I get it.

00:03:56.090 --> 00:03:56.923
So that's one pressure.

00:03:56.923 --> 00:03:58.130
- Their wrong.

00:03:58.130 --> 00:04:01.330
I understand, their gonna lose.

00:04:01.330 --> 00:04:02.900
What they don't understand

00:04:02.900 --> 00:04:05.730
is how quickly the world is evolving

00:04:05.730 --> 00:04:09.580
and how we're all more connected than ever

00:04:09.580 --> 00:04:11.530
and we're all looking
at each others cultures.

00:04:11.530 --> 00:04:12.540
I think the greatest thing

00:04:12.540 --> 00:04:15.883
that is ever gonna happen to
America is China's emergence.

00:04:17.170 --> 00:04:20.450
I think kids that are gonna
be born 10 years from now

00:04:20.450 --> 00:04:23.550
are gonna be winners in
America 40 years from now,

00:04:23.550 --> 00:04:25.747
because of the chip on their shoulder

00:04:25.747 --> 00:04:28.600
of loosing that world stage leadership.

00:04:28.600 --> 00:04:31.999
- So what should parents
invest in their kids,

00:04:31.999 --> 00:04:32.832
like what aspect?

00:04:32.832 --> 00:04:33.665
- One thing I would tell parents,

00:04:33.665 --> 00:04:35.607
is do a lot more listening

00:04:35.607 --> 00:04:38.187
and don't listen to your fuckin' friends.

00:04:38.187 --> 00:04:40.517
(laughing and clapping)

00:04:40.517 --> 00:04:44.000
Listen to your kids, and
when I say listening,

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:46.570
watch them, what do
they gravitate towards?

00:04:46.570 --> 00:04:49.020
Nobody thought playing
video games 20 years ago

00:04:49.020 --> 00:04:51.610
was gonna lead to a
luxurious financial life.

00:04:51.610 --> 00:04:53.208
It clearly has.

00:04:53.208 --> 00:04:55.625
(soft music)

